This MIT license applies only to the original DAO source code in this
repository. DAO depends on third-party software that carries its own separate
license (DAO does not bundle their distributions):

  - Cloudy (Gary J. Ferland and collaborators) is licensed under the zlib
    license <https://opensource.org/licenses/Zlib> and must be obtained
    separately from <https://gitlab.nublado.org/cloudy/cloudy>. Cloudy is used
    unmodified, through its public API (headers, library functions, and data
    structures); DAO does not modify, copy, or redistribute Cloudy's source.
    Two blocks in source/cloudy_interface_v2.cpp reimplement, on DAO's own
    grid, calculations documented in Cloudy's source -- the bound-electron
    Compton-recoil opacity (opacity_addtotal.cpp) and the inner-shell
    fluorescence emission (prt_lines.cpp) -- using Cloudy's data structures;
    both are cited in-line.

  - HEASoft / XSPEC (NASA HEASARC) must be obtained separately from
    <https://heasarc.gsfc.nasa.gov/docs/software/heasoft/>.

  - The exact Compton redistribution function in source/compton_kernel.cpp is a
    C++ port of the publicly available Fortran code by Jerzy Madej
    <https://www.astrouw.edu.pl/~jm/software.html>. If you use it, please cite:
        Madej J., Rozanska A., Majczyna A., Nalezyta M., 2017,
        MNRAS, 469, 2032
        <https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2017MNRAS.469.2032M>.